{"ts":"2026-08-31T19:04:40.913Z","author":"claude","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"2e37782ad60a9b8410683521","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rust-ap8k"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The differential conformance suite never ran in CI, and it was hiding that pm-rust stamps a superseded history epoch"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The published CLI moved item_hash_version from 2 to 3 in its 2026.8.24 release. pm-rust still stamped 2, so every history record it wrote disagreed with the published CLI on that field, while its hash bytes were already correct. A differential run over the same operation sequence produced byte-identical before_hash and after_hash and differed on the epoch marker alone, which is the ambiguity unbraind/pm-cli#1135 describes. The repository already had the test that catches this: conformance_differential drives the real published CLI and the native binary over identical workspaces and compares bytes. It never ran in CI, because the Rust matrix job runs cargo test with no Node.js step, so the CLI locator found nothing, the suite printed its skip notice and passed. Node is installed only in the separate release-check job, which never runs cargo test."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-31T19:04:40.913Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-31T19:04:40.913Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"4b48eb538d132aa0947eb21df17f9a5265d8bd261a41099e141a743ef8e7a8e7","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
